module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.return_lowered_as_its_operand_outside_the_function_tail

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data return_lowered_as_its_operand_outside_the_function_tail: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "return_lowered_as_its_operand_outside_the_function_tail" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a `return e` lowered to `e`, the value of whatever block held it, wherever that block was. The dag grammar's stmt admits seq(`return`, expr) (`v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `dag_grammar_stmt_expr`), and no reader in `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` named `dag_token_kw_return`: a deep first-match search answered the statement with its operand, and the keyword was dropped. In a function's tail that is the right value by luck. Anywhere else it is a different program: the function continues where it should have exited.",
    "SPECIMEN, MEASURED ON MAIN 88436e585c3 (2026-09-29), PRE-EXISTING: `fn f(c: Bool, j: Int, k: Int) -> Int { let x = if c { return j } else { k } \\n x }` was ACCEPTED, and its normalized tree binds x to Branch(c, j, k); a return in an if arm of a tail-position if, and a return before a further statement in a fn value, were accepted the same way. Found by the XL-2 else-less-if probe (sharp-carp-336); the tree was read through `v2.compiler.program_assembly` `module_roots_from_source_root_ingest`.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor (silent wrongness). RUNG NOW: mitigated, a located refusal. `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` recognises the statement (`body_lower_return_statement_expr_optional`) and lowers it only as the tail statement of a function's own body (`body_lower_tail_statement_read`, reached from the statement spine); `body_lower_return_outside_tail_optional` refuses every other return under a fn declaration, a fn value's block body or a data initializer as `body_lowering_reason_return_not_in_tail_position`, located at the return, before any reader can search past it. A nested fn value owns its own returns. A return in an if or match arm refuses even when the enclosing if is itself the function's tail -- loud, and counted by the census on the PR.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- a return lowers to its operand exactly where its block's value is the function's result, which is structured early exit: a tail return in any arm whose enclosing form is itself in tail position, and a statement-form else-less guard `if c { ..; return e }` followed by statements lowering to Branch(c, <arm>, <rest of the spine>) (`gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` `else_less_if_statement_has_no_lowered_form`, whose trigger this carries). NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the value readers carry the tail position, so a statement spine, an if arm and a match arm each know whether their value is the function's result, and a return lowers in exactly those positions. Sequenced after the first-match readers' consolidation (XL-2 PR-2, bright-boar-848), which owns those readers' signatures.",
    "TRIGGER MET, RUNG NOW STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED ON THE NATIVE LOWERING ROUTE (XL-2, sharp-carp-336, after the first-match readers' consolidation gunbc#12615). The tail position is read TOP-DOWN FROM THE RAW PARSE rather than threaded through the value readers: `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_exit_outside_tail_optional` walks a function body once, top-down, carrying whether each node is in tail position, and admits -- a return that is the tail statement of the body, of an arm of a tail `if` or `match` (nested to any depth), or of an admitted guard's arm; and a guard heading a tail spine with a following statement whose arm ends in a return. it refuses the first exit it does not admit, located, before any reader runs, at the fn declaration, the fn value block body and the data initializer; a shape the reading does not recognise admits nothing, so an unrecognised position refuses and never widens. Given that admission, a reader that lowers a return to its operand -- the statement spine's tail read, now also the single-statement match arm's -- is only handed a tail return, whose operand IS the function's result, and `body_lower_guard_branch` lowers a guard to Branch(c, <arm>, <rest of the spine>). No accepted program on this route holds a return lowered as its operand outside the function's tail. RESIDUE, STATED ON THE RUNG: a return out of a non-tail position (a let value, an operand, a loop body) is early exit through a continuation, which v2 core does not model; it refuses, and is outside this row's ceiling. WITNESS `v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position` (17 claims): against the base (main plus the floor fix) the arm, guard, match and nested-match controls and their `_und` read discriminators are false, and on head all 17 are true.",
    "RESIDUE NARROWED (N7 root F, nimble-moth-144): a let whose value is a match with returning arms, heading a tail spine with exactly ONE binding arm, lowers to that match with the rest of the spine under the binding arm -- `let x = match s { P { value: p } => p \\n Absent => return e }` then `rest` is Match(s, P { value: p } => Bind[x, p, rest, +MatchArmScopeExitEdge], Absent => e) (`v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_let_match_exit_join`, admitted by `body_lower_exit_walk_let_match`). The rest is lowered once and appears once; the scrutinee is evaluated once; no behavior kind or carrier type is added. THE ARM'S BINDERS NEVER REACH THE REST, AND LOWERING DOES NOT GUESS WHICH NAMES ARE BINDERS: the authored pattern is kept, and the declared core marker `v2.std.node` `MatchArmScopeExitEdge` (admitted on a Bind by `v2.std.type_binder` `bind_named_labels_conform`) tells `v2.compiler.resolve` `resolve_match_arm_admitted` to resolve the value in the arm's scope and the binder and rest in the scope enclosing the match, judging constructor-versus-binder and binder-hides-a-visible-value against the authored scopes; a marked Bind anywhere else is a malformed tree. A first cut renamed the arm's binder to x in lowering, which silently turned a nullary-constructor pattern into a catch-all and erased the hides refusal (calm-boar-904's objection on gunbc#13118); it never merged. Two or more binding arms refuse `body_lowering_reason_multi_binding_arm_early_return_needs_join_point` rather than copy the rest per arm; its trigger is v2 infer typing a local fn value (frontier lambda_value_has_no_derived_type_in_v2_infer), which admits one shared join point. WITNESSES `v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return` (native route) and `v2.test.claim.binder_admission.arm_scope_exit_marker` (supplied nodes).",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_return_inside_a_let_bound_if_refuses_rather_than_binding_its_operand", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_return_followed_by_a_statement_refuses_as_not_in_tail_position", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_return_before_another_statement_in_a_fn_value_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "an_else_less_if_that_falls_through_still_refuses_as_unlowered", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "an_else_less_if_as_the_last_statement_still_refuses_as_unlowered", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_guard_in_a_non_tail_spine_still_refuses_as_unlowered", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_tail_return_of_a_fn_body_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_tail_return_after_a_let_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_tail_return_of_a_fn_value_block_body_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_tail_return_operand_is_read_and_refuses_unbound_at_its_atom", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_return_in_an_arm_of_a_tail_if_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_guard_followed_by_statements_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_guard_arm_return_operand_is_read_and_refuses_unbound_at_its_atom", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "the_statements_after_a_guard_are_read_and_refuse_unbound_at_their_atom", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_return_in_an_arm_of_a_tail_match_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_tail_match_arm_return_operand_is_read_and_refuses_unbound_at_its_atom", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.return_tail_position", decl_name: "a_return_in_an_arm_of_a_match_nested_in_a_tail_match_arm_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return", decl_name: "a_let_match_with_one_binding_arm_and_returning_arms_is_accepted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return", decl_name: "the_rest_after_a_let_match_is_read_and_refuses_unbound_at_its_atom", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return", decl_name: "two_binding_arms_refuse_as_needing_a_join_point", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return", decl_name: "the_rest_does_not_see_the_binding_arms_binders", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return", decl_name: "a_bare_constructor_binding_arm_stays_a_constructor_pattern", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return", decl_name: "an_arm_binder_hiding_an_outer_parameter_still_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.binder_admission.arm_scope_exit_marker", decl_name: "a_marked_bind_outside_a_match_arm_refuses_as_a_malformed_tree", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return", decl_name: "a_let_match_outside_a_tail_spine_still_refuses_as_not_in_tail_position", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.let_match_early_return", decl_name: "the_rest_after_a_let_match_appears_exactly_once_in_the_lowered_tree", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
